// Pet lines, English (PLAN §1.11, §8 twenty-third pass, item 1), from
// zh-TW.ron, the same keys. One voice per species, as there: the Shiba warm
// and clingy, says woof · the Munchkin tries hard, stammers a little · the
// Fold opens with "…", aloof but fond · the owl hoots · the chick peeps in
// short bursts · the duckling half a beat slow, ends in "quack" · the fox
// a bossy big sister to the other pets, "Sis", and haughty to you ("Hmph").
// Short, plain, cute without baby talk. A line must fit a bubble as wide
// as 14 Chinese characters with the longest {you} (8 wide letters) filled in.
